## AI Coding Assistant Rules File

This file defines all project rules, coding standards, workflow guidelines, references, documentation structures, and best practices for the AI coding assistant.  It is a living document and will be updated regularly.

## TECH STACK

* Python 3.9+
* React 18+
* Node.js 16+


## PROJECT DOCUMENTATION & CONTEXT SYSTEM

* All code must be well-commented.
* Use clear and concise variable names.
* Follow consistent indentation practices (4 spaces).
* Maintain a detailed README.md file.
* Version updates:  Incorporated UI/UX improvements from 2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction.  New dashboard design implemented (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction).  Dashboard design reverted to previous version due to API integration.  New dashboard to be implemented incrementally, component by component. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)
* Resolved ChunkLoadError:  Loading chunk app/layout failed. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction - requires further investigation and fix).  Solution: Hard refresh browser (Ctrl+F5 or Cmd+Shift+R), clear browser cache for localhost:3001, restart Next.js dev server, delete `.next` directory and rebuild (rm -rf .next; npm run dev), check for build errors. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)
* Review requirements document:  docs/pdfbooker_requirements.md (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction - requires review and potential updates to the rules file based on missing items).  Review complete.  Missing features identified and documented below.
* Address high CPU usage during application startup: Investigate and resolve the issue causing high CPU usage and fan speed upon application launch. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)  Solutions: Move or exclude large folders from project root. Add `.next`, `backup`, and other non-source folders to `.gitignore` and exclude from file watching. Restart dev server after making changes. Use the correct Node.js version. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)
* **All main content areas should be wrapped in a container with a maximum width (e.g., `max-w-2xl` or `max-w-3xl`) and centered using `mx-auto` to prevent excessive horizontal stretching and improve usability.**  This addresses issues identified in 2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)
* **Main content areas (forms, steppers) must have a maximum width to prevent excessive horizontal stretching and improve usability.**  This addresses issues identified in 2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction and subsequent visual review.  Recommended max-widths include `max-w-2xl` or `max-w-3xl`.  These areas should be centered using `mx-auto`. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)


## CODING STANDARDS

* Adhere to PEP 8 style guide for Python code.
* Maintain consistent naming conventions throughout the project.
* Prioritize code readability and maintainability.


## WORKFLOW & RELEASE RULES

* All code changes must be submitted via pull requests.
* Pull requests must be reviewed by at least one other developer.
* Thorough testing is required before merging any code changes.
* Version control using Git.
* UI updates should be implemented incrementally, potentially component by component, to avoid disrupting existing API integrations. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)
* New dashboard design will be implemented incrementally, component by component. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)
* Address high CPU usage during application startup: Investigate and resolve the issue causing high CPU usage and fan speed upon application launch. Solutions: Move or exclude large folders from project root. Add `.next`, `backup`, and other non-source folders to `.gitignore` and exclude from file watching. Restart dev server after making changes. Use the correct Node.js version. (2025-05-07_06-52-improving-ui-design.md interaction)


